||| Build-time selection of the (device, dtype) pair the Idris unit
||| test suite targets. Generated from this template by the Makefile
||| rule at `Makefile`'s TESTCONFIG_IDR target — observes `PRIMARY`
||| (and the MLX_DEVICE / TORCH_DEVICE envs for hardware-variant
||| selection) and substitutes the chosen tags into this template via
||| sed. Same trick as the example-side `BuildConfig.idr` and per-build
||| `HwConfig.idr`; the test ipkg can't import either of those (they
||| live in `idris-ml-examples` / generated downstream of `Tensor`),
||| so the test sourcedir gets its own copy.
|||
||| Selection matrix (PRIMARY × hw-device env → TestExecutor, TestDType):
|||
|||   tape, *                     → TapeExecutor,              F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cpu      → TorchExecutor TCpu,        F64
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=mps      → TorchExecutor TMps,        F32
|||   torch, TORCH_DEVICE=cuda     → TorchExecutor (TCuda 0),   F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=cpu          → MlxExecutor MCpu,          F64
|||   mlx, MLX_DEVICE=gpu          → MlxExecutor MGpu,          F32
|||
||| Pre-existing unit tests (GradMode / ManagedHandle / …) used to pin
||| `{d=TapeExecutor}` directly; that bound them to a tape-linked dylib and
||| made `make BACKEND=torch test` / `BACKEND=mlx test` fail at FFI
||| resolution with `no entry for "tensor_create_scalar_tape"`. Tests
||| now spell `{d=TestExecutor}` and resolve to the active primary at
||| build time.
|||
||| Idris-2 cannot drive type-level selection from a runtime env var —
||| types are fixed at elaboration. The generated `TestConfig.idr` is
||| in `.gitignore`. Do not edit the generated file directly; edit
||| this `.in` template instead.
module Test.Config

import public Executor
import public Executor.Tape
import public Executor.Torch
import public Executor.Mlx

||| Executor tag the unit tests target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
TestExecutor : Type
TestExecutor = @DEVICE@

||| DType tag the unit tests target. See the Selection matrix in the
||| module docstring.
public export
TestDType : DType
TestDType = @DTYPE@

||| Lowercase name of the primary backend ("tape" / "torch" / "mlx"),
||| as seen at TestConfig generation time. Value-level mirror of the
||| Type-level `TestExecutor` selection above. Tests that need to gate
||| at runtime — e.g. F32-vs-F64 paired-oracle tests that only make
||| sense when both dtypes are admissible on the active device — read
||| this string to decide whether to run or skip.
public export
TestPrimaryBackend : String
TestPrimaryBackend = "@PRIMARY@"
